.TH HTTP_STRERROR 3
.SH NAME
http_strerror \- text of the last error of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "const char* http_strerror(http* " h ", int " ret ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_strerror ()
describes the error of an operation that returned
.IR ret .
If
.I ret
is -1 the text is that of the TLS error of the connection when TLS is used, otherwise that
of
.I errno
(as strerror(3)). For any other value it returns "success".
.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to a text that must not be changed or freed.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canread(3), http_canwrite(3), tls_strerror(3)
